  "title": "Chapter 7: Tripura Polity — Constitution, Governance & Administration",
  "order": 7,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "xobr76l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.1 Constitutional Provisions for Tripura"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Tripura attained full statehood on January 21, 1972, under the North-Eastern Areas (Reorganisation) Act, 1971.",
        "The Tripura Legislative Assembly is unicameral and consists of 60 elected members, with 20 seats reserved for Scheduled Tribes.",
        "The Tripura Tribal Areas Autonomous District Council (TTAADC) operates under the Sixth Schedule of the Constitution of India.",
        "Administratively, the state is divided into 8 districts, 23 subdivisions, and 58 development blocks."
      ],
      "id": "846vn9s"
    },
